6. Non-OSI / proprietary
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    mkl  2024.2.2  Copyright (C) Intel Corporation
                   Intel Simplified Software License (October 2022)
                   https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/license/onemkl-license-faq.html

Intel Math Kernel Library. It is NOT used at runtime: `environment.yml` pins the
OpenBLAS build of the BLAS/LAPACK stack (`libblas=3.9.0=*openblas*`), and in the
image `lib/libblas.so.3` resolves to `libopenblasp-r0.3.28.so`, which is what
NumPy loads. MKL is nevertheless installed, because the conda-forge OpenBLAS
build of `libblas` declares `mkl` among its dependencies — so roughly 125 MB of
it is redistributed in the image without ever being exercised.


